{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Pre-review citation sweep against current `origin/main`. This description's cites are pinned to `083620b0`, now **333 commits** behind. One blocking finding, one scope correction, plus line drift.\n\n## 1. AC2 names two files that no longer exist — BLOCKING\n\nAC2 requires `tests/scripts/test_store_snapshot_io_seam_clean_heldout.py` and `tests/scripts/test_cli_seam_clean_heldout.py` to be \"green with `read-via` marker counts as budgeted\". Neither file exists on `origin/main`. There is no `tests/scripts/*seam*` file at all, no `*seam_clean*` path anywhere in the tree, and **`_TOTAL_MARKER_CAP` does not appear in any file**. The Approach's \"Budgets:\" bullet — drop the hlc row and set `_TOTAL_MARKER_CAP = 3`; drop the compact_txn row and set `_TOTAL_MARKER_CAP = 1` — has no target.\n\nThe `# read-via:` idiom itself is alive and well: 23 source files carry markers, including both of this story's (`src/rebar/_store/hlc.py:42` `# read-via: test-only-clock-injection` and `src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:187` `# read-via: test-failpoint`). What changed is the enforcement. The surviving marker gates are `scripts/check_config_reads.py` and `scripts/check_config_ownership.py`, tested by `tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads.py`, `test_check_config_reads_heldout.py`, `test_check_config_reads_red_proof.py`, and `test_check_config_ownership.py`. That gate is scoped to **config-schema fields** — it reports `<schema_path>:<lineno>: <cls>.<field>` and requires a pointer on a declared-but-unread field — so on its face it does not govern the two env-read markers this story removes.\n\nBefore re-requesting review, establish which is true and rewrite AC2 accordingly:\n- if no gate counts these two markers, the Budgets bullet and AC2 are simply **moot** and should be deleted rather than re-pointed; or\n- if some gate does govern them, name that gate and its real assertion.\n\nDeleting a marker is in any case the safe direction for a counting gate, so this is unlikely to be real work — but AC2 as written is red on a correct implementation because the files it names cannot be made green.\n\n## 2. AC1 is satisfiable — confirmed\n\n`git grep -n 'REBAR_HLC_NOW\\|REBAR_TEST_COMPACT_RENAME_BARRIER' -- src` currently returns exactly 5 hits, all genuinely this story's and all removable:\n\n- `src/rebar/_store/hlc.py:19` (module docstring), `:39` (`physical_now` docstring), `:42` (the `os.environ.get` read)\n- `src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:180` (docstring), `:187` (the read)\n\nThe grep is `src`-scoped, so the mentions in `docs/remediation-implementation-plan.md:554,582` do not threaten it. Those two are historical planning prose describing the skewed-clock harness; leaving them is correct, but worth a deliberate decision rather than an accident.\n\n## 3. The test-flip this story depends on is real, and currently asserts the opposite\n\n`tests/unit/test_hlc.py:91` asserts `re.search(r\"\\bREBAR_HLC_NOW\\b\", source)` — that the env name **is** present in the source. The plan correctly anticipates replacing it with an `os\\.environ`-absent assertion; recording the exact current line so the flip is mechanical. Cited as `:89-94`, actually `:91`.\n\n## 4. Line drift (substance verified intact)\n\n| Cited | Actual on `origin/main` |\n|---|---|\n| `hlc.py:57-67` reads `REBAR_HLC_NOW` | `:42`; docstrings `:19`, `:39` |\n| `hlc.py:36-37` docstring sentence | `:39` |\n| `compact_txn.py:179-195` | `:180-187` |\n| `test_hlc.py:33-77` setters | `:33,39,48,58,67,77` — range correct |\n| `test_cli_js_safe_integers.py:91` | `:74` |\n| `test_export_ndjson_js_safe.py:96` | `:96` — correct |\n| `test_compact_process_death.py:101` | `:101` — correct |\n| `test_concurrency_regression.py:599` | `:521` |\n| `test_concurrency_regression.py:1693-1811` | setters at `:1585,1588-1590,1606,1622,1663,1679,1697` |\n| `test_concurrency_regression.py:596-602,1637-1646` | `:519-521`, `:1537,1585` |\n| `docs/env-vars.md:57,160` | `:59`, `:144` |\n| `.github/mechanism-baseline.json:505,608` | `:495`, `:579` |\n| `detect_ci.py::detect_test_helpers` | `scripts/_mechanism_delta/detect_ci.py:115` — exists, shape claim holds |\n\nThe `hlc.py:125,130` / `compact.py:253` / `compact_trigger.py:113` / `compact_txn.py:469` out-of-scope cites were not re-measured; do that with the rest.\n\n## Base stability\n\n`ed5a` and `cb2b` (this story's dependency chain) touch no file in this story's scope, so citations re-measured on current `origin/main` remain valid as those land — with the exception of anything `cb2b` moves in `docs/env-vars.md`, which both stories edit. Re-measure `docs/env-vars.md` line numbers after `cb2b` lands, not before."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793421414032523679,"uuid":"8b3fc03b-3989-4a83-a051-a35477c06a91"}